  <title>Unit 3 Overview and Readiness</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00667</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Unit 3 Overview and Readiness</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d7fab56a-22fd-449d-94f5-f258a99067f1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this unit, students will:</para>
<list>
  <item>Write, with and without technology, linear functions that provide a reasonable fit to data to estimate solutions and make predictions for real-world problems.</item>
  <item>Calculate, using technology, the correlation coefficient between two quantitative variables and interpret this quantity as a measure of the strength of the linear association.</item>
  <item>Compare and contrast association and causation in real-world problems.</item>
</list>
<para>To accomplish these unit-level learning goals, students will complete the following lessons and activities.</para>
<title>Student Readiness for Unit 3</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, students will need to be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Distinguish linear patterns from nonlinear patterns based on scatter plots.</item>
  <item>Identify positive and negative trends in a scatter plot.</item>
  <item>Interpret slopes and \(y\)-intercepts of graphs of linear equations.</item>
</list>
<para>This Unit Overview Video will provide a big picture look at the content found in this unit as well as the prerequisite skills that students need for accessing the content in the unit.</para>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
